# Frontend UX Rules

- Design for layman clarity: use plain labels and short helper text.
- For AI surfaces, show confidence + short reason when suggesting actions.
- Use progressive disclosure for advanced options ("More options"), not crowded forms.
- One primary action per screen section.
- Replace mock fallback behavior with loading/empty states in critical flows.
- Preserve journaling feel for AI input: large, subtle, low-contrast controls.
